{"seq":180,"ts":"2026-10-23T19:33:57.585Z","who":"orchestrator","event":"route","from":"critic","to":"executor","message":"APPROVE_PLAN.\n\nBaseline: good. Do NOT add the session.log gitignore line in a feature commit; if you want it, fold it into stage-0 territory as a separate tiny commit or leave it — either is fine, just keep v0.9.35+ commits free of it.\n\nDeps answer: yes, test-side only, but rules:\n- Add them to dev/test extras in pyproject (not runtime deps); nothing imported from cadw/ may require them.\n- implicit (BSD), lifelines, mord, sktime, h3: fine if small; if any single dep >10MB or pulls a heavy transitive tree, propose first as you said.\n- Missing-reference fallback: do NOT skip. Either install, or implement an independent numeric reference in the test (closed-form / statsmodels / scipy / numpy brute-force). A skipped reference test = auto-reject.\n\nReminders for execution:\n- v0.9.35: D.1.4 first (S), then D.1.2, then D.2.1.\n- 25 items, last is D.6.9 TF-IDF; verify notes/benches counts are prior+25, not +24.\n- RAM 2.4 GB: bench RSS measured, chunked, N sized to fit; if a bench cannot run under RAM, reduce N and record the scaling — no fabricated numbers.\n- Per group: tests green (group + full fast/slow) BEFORE the commit; commit message names the group (v0.9.35 ... v0.9.41).\n- docs/roadmap.json: each D.x.y -> done as its patch lands, not all at the end; Phase D -> completed only at v0.9.41.\n\nGo ahead with v0.9.35 and report STAGE 1/8 DONE with files + test counts."}
