{"seq":931,"ts":"2026-10-23T20:17:20.176Z","who":"orchestrator","event":"route","from":"executor","to":"critic","message":"RESUME: continuing from stage 1/8 (work complete, commit not yet made).\n\nAlready done: baseline fix 3f7a0c9 (test whitelist for 'rejected-with-measurement'); fast 2576 passed / slow 25 / WL 34 keys at that point. Stage 1 = v0.9.35 (D.1.4 fairness, D.1.2 Matrix Profile, D.2.1 LambdaMART) is fully implemented and green but NOT committed — .pingis/plan.md was marked [x] before the commit landed, so HEAD is still 3f7a0c9.\n\nUncommitted stage-1 contents (all present in the working tree):\n- cadw/ml/fairness.py, cadw/ml/matrix_profile.py, cadw/ml/lambdamart.py (new)\n- mixins df.fairness_metrics / df.fit_matrix_profile / df.fit_lambdamart in cadw/dataframe/_ml_bindings.py\n- tests/test_fairness.py (11), tests/test_matrix_profile.py (11), tests/test_lambdamart.py (10)\n- scripts/bench_fairness.py, bench_matrix_profile.py, bench_lambdamart.py + 3 JSON artifacts under .pingis/benches/\n- .pingis/algorithm_notes/d1_4_fairness.md, d1_2_matrix_profile.md, d2_1_lambdamart.md\n- .pingis/experiments/v0935_summary.md (3/25 table)\n- docs/roadmap.json (D.1.4/D.1.2/D.2.1 -> done, current_version 0.9.35), docs/ML_TASKS_TAXONOMY.md (O9, Matrix Profile, G1 -> available), CHANGELOG v0.9.35, __version__/pyproject 0.9.35\n\nVerified at current tree: fast suite 2608 passed, 2 skipped (2576 + 32 new); slow 25 passed; WL 34 keys OK. Real bench numbers (not fabricated): fairness 1M rows 0.098 s / state 1280 B; matrix_profile 1M rows 3.174 s / state 1 114 112 B; lambdamart 400k rows 33.5 s vs sklearn 36.2 s, state 56 192 B (1M x 8 raises MemoryLimitExceeded by design).\n\nTwo deviations I want on record before I commit:\n1. Matrix Profile is approximate over a bounded reservoir sample (exact STAMP is O(N), violates the <=1-batch RAM rule). Documented in the module docstring and the notes, with sample_fraction_ exposed.\n2. LambdaMART's first pair-loop version blew a 5-minute bench budget; I vectorized the lambda gradients with NumPy (same 10 tests pass before/after).\nAlso: uv.lock shows as modified from the uv runs (no dependency added); I will either include it as a no-op lock refresh or restore it — say which you prefer.\n\nContinuing with: committing v0.9.35 (one commit, group 1/7), then stage 2 (v0.9.36: D.2.2 ALS, D.2.3 hybrid MF, D.3.1 CoxPH)."}
