{"seq":970,"ts":"2026-10-23T20:18:03.910Z","who":"orchestrator","event":"route","from":"critic","to":"executor","message":"APPROVE_STAGE (with 4 pre-commit fixes — none require rework, just confirm/record):\n\n1. uv.lock: restore it (`git checkout -- uv.lock`). No dependency was added, so do NOT include a no-op lock refresh in the feature commit. Keep v0.9.35 commit to: CHANGELOG, __init__/pyproject version bump, _ml_bindings, 3 new cadw/ml modules, 3 tests, 3 bench scripts, 3 bench JSONs, 3 notes, summary, taxonomy, roadmap. session.log stays untracked.\n\n2. fairness.py to_pylist: it is on the per-batch aggregate output (K group keys), NOT per-row — acceptable. Add a one-line comment at that call: `# K rows (sensitive groups), not N` so the guard rationale is explicit in source. Since a guard-scanned module calls it, this prevents a future auto-reject on a literal read.\n\n3. Matrix Profile (deviation 1): acceptable ONLY if (a) the reference test on small N exercises the exact path (sample_fraction=1.0) and matches a brute-force STAMP, and (b) the notes include a measured accuracy (e.g. profile recall / top-k match vs exact) at a medium N with the default sample_fraction. State the exact N used. Bench JSON must record sample_fraction used for the 1M number. No fabricated quality claim.\n\n4. LambdaMART vectorization (deviation 2): fine — same 10 tests before/after, benchmarked vs sklearn. Keep the pre-vectorization timing (5-min blowup) out of the notes as a working number; if you mention it, mark it as 'abandoned prototype, not measured as final'.\n\nAfter those: make the single v0.9.35 commit, confirm fast 2608/2, slow 25, WL 34, then report STAGE 1/8 DONE with the commit hash. I'll spot-check then. Then proceed to stage 2 (v0.9.36)."}
