{"seq":1079,"ts":"2026-10-23T20:38:56.813Z","who":"orchestrator","event":"route","from":"executor","to":"critic","message":"RESUME: continuing from stage 2/8.\n\nAlready done: stage 1 (v0.9.35: D.1.4 fairness, D.1.2 Matrix Profile, D.2.1 LambdaMART) is implemented, all 4 of your pre-commit fixes applied, and suites verified green (fast 2608 passed / 2 skipped after my last full run; slow 25; WL 34 keys; 33 algorithm tests pass). BUT the single v0.9.35 commit is NOT yet made — HEAD is still 3f7a0c9 and the stage-1 files are uncommitted in the tree. That is the one gap from my last report.\n\nYour 4 fixes, all applied:\n1. uv.lock restored (now shows modified only because of later uv runs — will restore again before commit).\n2. fairness.py has the `# K rows (sensitive groups), not N` comment above the K-sized to_pylist.\n3. Matrix Profile: added test_exact_path_matches_bruteforce_stamp (frac=1.0, bit-identical to brute-force STAMP, maxdiff 0.00e+00, 12 tests now). Measured sampled-path accuracy recorded in the notes at N=3000, w=16, S=512, frac=0.1715: top-10 overlap 0/10, top-50 1/50, top-100 6/100, MAE 0.804. Reported as a weak result, with D.1.2 explicitly labelled exact-on-sample rather than a STAMP replacement. Bench JSON already records sample_fraction (0.041 / 0.0041).\n4. LambdaMART notes: the abandoned pair-loop prototype is no longer given as a measured number.\n\nPLAN for stages 2-8 is unchanged and as previously approved: v0.9.36 (ALS, hybrid MF, CoxPH) -> v0.9.37 -> v0.9.38 -> v0.9.39 -> v0.9.40 -> v0.9.41 (ending D.6.9 TF-IDF) -> final verification, one commit per group.\n\nRequesting APPROVE_PLAN to (a) make the v0.9.35 commit first, then (b) continue with stage 2 (v0.9.36)."}
