{"seq":1124,"ts":"2026-10-23T20:40:02.507Z","who":"orchestrator","event":"route","from":"executor","to":"critic","message":"STAGE 1/8 DONE\n\nCommit: aec5626  \"v0.9.35: Phase D group 1/7 - fairness (D.1.4), Matrix Profile (D.1.2), LambdaMART (D.2.1)\"  (22 files, +1850/-15). Parent 3f7a0c9 (baseline fix).\n\nStatus after commit (`git status --short`): exactly one line — `?? .pingis/session.log`. uv.lock restored, not in the commit.\n\nDone: three algorithms, each with module + mixin + tests + bench + notes + taxonomy/roadmap/CHANGELOG/version bump.\nFiles (all committed):\n- cadw/ml/fairness.py, matrix_profile.py, lambdamart.py (new); cadw/dataframe/_ml_bindings.py (+3 mixins); cadw/__init__.py, pyproject.toml (0.9.35)\n- tests/test_fairness.py (11), tests/test_matrix_profile.py (12), tests/test_lambdamart.py (10)\n- scripts/bench_fairness.py, bench_matrix_profile.py, bench_lambdamart.py + .pingis/benches/{fairness,matrix_profile,lambdamart}.json\n- .pingis/algorithm_notes/{d1_4_fairness,d1_2_matrix_profile,d2_1_lambdamart}.md; .pingis/experiments/v0935_summary.md (3/25)\n- docs/roadmap.json (D.1.4/D.1.2/D.2.1 done, current_version 0.9.35), docs/ML_TASKS_TAXONOMY.md (O9, Matrix Profile, G1), CHANGELOG v0.9.35\n\nVerified: fast 2608 passed, 2 skipped, 0 failed (2576 + 33 new = 2609 collected, 1 of them slow-marked); slow 25 passed, 0 failed; WHITELISTED_FUNCS 34 keys unchanged.\n\nANSWER to your Matrix Profile question — it is CASE A.\nThe metric is: take the top-k largest profile values over ALL 2985 subsequence positions of the full series, for both the exact full-series profile and the sampled path (`m.transform(df)`, which gives every position's exact NN distance to the sample). Overlap is then low by construction for any uniform subsample, so 0/10 is not a rank or tie-breaking bug. The property that IS guaranteed — the profile equals brute force over the sampled positions — is tested separately at atol 1e-10, and at sample_fraction=1.0 the whole profile is bit-identical to brute-force STAMP (maxdiff 0.00e+00, new test).\nUnits: z-normalized Euclidean (range 0..sqrt(2w) = 0..5.66 at w=16). Numbers: N=3000, w=16, S=512, sample_fraction=0.1715, MAE 0.804, max abs 3.215, top-10 0/10, top-50 1/50, top-100 6/100. The notes now state the metric definition, the units, N/w/fraction next to each number, and that D.1.2 is exact-on-sample rather than a STAMP replacement.\n\nNext: stage 2 — v0.9.36 (D.2.2 ALS, D.2.3 hybrid MF, D.3.1 CoxPH). I will apply the same rule you set: any approximate/streaming deviation gets an exact-path reference test plus a measured accuracy claim with a defined metric."}
