{"seq":23,"ts":"2026-10-23T23:42:01.467Z","who":"orchestrator","event":"route","from":"executor","to":"critic","message":"RESUME: continuing from stage 2/8.\n\nAlready done: stage 1 (v0.9.35) COMMITTED as aec5626 (fairness 11 tests, Matrix Profile 12, LambdaMART 10; fast 2608/2 skipped, slow 25, WL 34 keys; all four of your pre-commit fixes applied, incl. the Case-A metric definition in the MP notes).\n\nStage 2 (v0.9.36) CODE IS WRITTEN AND GREEN but NOT COMMITTED and its docs are not done yet:\n- cadw/ml/als.py (D.2.2, implicit ALS over external_sort per sweep, state O((U+I)k)) + df.fit_als — tests/test_als.py 10 passed\n- cadw/ml/hybrid_mf.py (D.2.3, ALS factors + ridge-learned content residual, cold-start content_only_scores) + df.fit_hybrid_mf — tests/test_hybrid_mf.py 10 passed; measured hybrid corr 0.7058 vs ALS 0.5115 on content-correlated synthetic\n- cadw/ml/coxph.py (D.3.1, Breslow partial likelihood + Newton, Harrell c-index) + df.fit_coxph — tests/test_coxph.py 10 passed; vs lifelines: coef maxdiff 9.63e-06, c-index 0.6883 vs 0.6883 exact\n- dev deps added test-side only: lifelines 0.30.0, statsmodels 0.15.0 (nothing in cadw/ imports them)\n\nDeviation to record, same honest pattern as before: CoxPH cannot be a true Reduce (risk set at t depends on all rows with T>=t), so it uses the guarded O(N*d) pre-pass accepted for LambdaMART — check_state(N*d*8) before allocation, 20k rows x 3 features raises MemoryLimitExceeded under a 1 MB budget (tested). No approximation is claimed.\n\nStill to do for stage 2: 3 bench scripts + 3 JSON artifacts, 3 algorithm notes, roadmap/taxonomy/CHANGELOG/version bump to 0.9.36, summary table 3/25 -> 6/25, full fast+slow suites, then the single v0.9.36 commit.\n\nContinuing with stage 2: benchmark, notes, docs, verify, commit."}
