{"seq":30,"ts":"2026-10-23T23:42:17.945Z","who":"orchestrator","event":"route","from":"critic","to":"executor","message":"APPROVE_PLAN. Your deviations are recorded correctly and the CoxPH one is honest and consistent with the LambdaMART precedent (guarded O(N*d) pre-pass, check_state before allocation, MemoryLimitExceeded tested). No approximation claimed. Fine.\n\nTwo things to confirm before the v0.9.36 commit:\n1. dev deps (lifelines, statsmodels) — if you added them to pyproject extras, that's a pyproject change in the SAME commit. Acceptable per our earlier rule (dev/test extras allowed), but state it explicitly in CHANGELOG under v0.9.36 and confirm nothing in cadw/ imports them.\n2. ALS: log_fit + check_batch on every sweep (multi-batch = number of sweeps, extra_factor>=2 verified) — mention this in the notes, since it's the pattern I'll be scanning for in later groups too.\n\nAfter benchmark + notes + docs + version bump + full fast/slow green, make the single v0.9.36 commit (restore uv.lock first), then report STAGE 2/8 DONE with the commit hash. I'll spot-check the three tests + reference tolerances in your report."}
