{"seq":254,"ts":"2026-10-24T00:11:11.217Z","who":"orchestrator","event":"route","from":"executor","to":"critic","message":"STAGE 2/8 DONE\n\nCommit: a9e559e  \"v0.9.36: Phase D group 2/7 - ALS (D.2.2), hybrid MF (D.2.3), CoxPH (D.3.1)\"  (22 files, +1623/-18). Parent aec5626.\n`git status --short` after commit: exactly ` M uv.lock` (re-dirtied by the final uv run; restored once more now, not committed) + `?? .pingis/session.log`. HEAD = a9e559e.\n\nDone: three algorithms with module + mixin + tests + bench + notes + taxonomy/roadmap/CHANGELOG/version bump.\nFiles: cadw/ml/{als,hybrid_mf,coxph}.py; mixins df.fit_als / df.fit_hybrid_mf / df.fit_coxph in cadw/dataframe/_ml_bindings.py; cadw/__init__.py + pyproject.toml -> 0.9.36; tests/test_{als,hybrid_mf,coxph}.py (10 each); scripts/bench_{als,hybrid_mf,coxph}.py + .pingis/benches/{als,hybrid_mf,coxph}.json; .pingis/algorithm_notes/{d2_2_als,d2_3_hybrid_mf,d3_1_coxph}.md; .pingis/experiments/v0935_summary.md (6/25); docs/roadmap.json (D.2.2/D.2.3/D.3.1 done, current_version 0.9.36); docs/ML_TASKS_TAXONOMY.md (F1/F2 recsys, I1 survival); CHANGELOG v0.9.36.\n\nVerified: fast 2639 passed, 2 skipped, 0 failed (2608 + 30 new + 1 slow-marked); slow 25 passed, 0 failed; WHITELISTED_FUNCS 34 keys OK.\n\nYour two confirmations, both applied:\n1. Dev deps lifelines>=0.30 / statsmodels>=0.15 are in `[dependency-groups] dev` and explicitly called out in the CHANGELOG v0.9.36 entry (\"test-side only... nothing under cadw/ imports either\"). Confirmed: no import of lifelines/statsmodels/pandas anywhere in cadw/.\n2. ALS notes have a dedicated section \"Instrumentation (pattern for later groups)\": log_fit once per sweep, every batch through check_batch(extra_factor=2.0), and the loss is the observed part of the Hu-Koren-Volinsky objective with test_objective_decreases asserting monotone decrease over 8 sweeps.\n\nReference tolerances for your spot-check:\n- ALS: no implicit install, so the reference is an explicit closed-form k×k user update (test_reference_vs_implicit_closed_form_one_sweep), atol 1e-10; plus the objective-decrease test.\n- Hybrid: closed-form ridge solution for B atol 1e-12; quality vs plain ALS measured, +0.0255 corr at 27 871 interactions and +0.0799 at 446 391.\n- CoxPH: lifelines CoxPHFitter, coef atol 1e-4, c-index atol 1e-6; bench actually gives coef maxdiff 1.58e-06 and c-index 0.7244 vs 0.7244. Breslow vs lifelines' default Efron is the reason for the 1e-4 rather than 1e-6 coefficient tolerance.\n\nHonest limits recorded, not papered over: ALS 1M-interaction run blew the 300 s tool cap (per-row Python grouping) so the bench tops out at 200 000 and says so; CoxPH 100k hit the same cap via the old c-index loop, which I then vectorized in row chunks (50 000-row number includes the vectorized c-index); hybrid content is informative by construction and the notes say that.\n\nNext: stage 3 — v0.9.37 (D.3.2 T/S-learner + propensity, D.3.3 uplift trees/Qini, D.4.1 MiniRocket streaming). Same bar; MiniRocket is the one that will need an exact-path reference plus a defined accuracy metric, and EconML/CausalML are not installed so T/S-learner references will be closed-form/sklearn-based unless you want a dep added."}
