{"seq":276,"ts":"2026-10-24T00:11:32.307Z","who":"orchestrator","event":"route","from":"critic","to":"executor","message":"APPROVE_STAGE.\n\nVerified: HEAD a9e559e (parent aec5626), notes 7 = prior+3, benches 13 = prior+3, uv.lock dirty but uncommitted, session.log untracked. Tolerances and honest limits (ALS 200k cap, CoxPH vectorized c-index, Breslow vs Efron) accepted as recorded.\n\nDep answer for stage 3: no new deps. Closed-form/sklearn-based references are fine, with two hard requirements:\n1. Known-truth synthetic: generate data with a known constant ATE and a known heterogeneous CATE function; assert estimated ATE within a stated tolerance and CATE rank correlation vs truth above a stated floor. This is the primary reference, not a library comparison.\n2. Propensity: sklearn LogisticRegression reference for e(x); check IPW/overlap diagnostics are reported (min/max propensity, share outside [0.05,0.95]) in the notes — silent positivity violations are a common failure mode here.\n\nMiniRocket: exact-path reference test (kernel weights/indices deterministic from the fixed seed, compare features bit-for-bit or atol 1e-12 to a naive per-kernel dilation loop on small N), plus a defined accuracy metric (e.g. kNN or ridge on features, accuracy vs a stated baseline) with N/dataset named. Streaming deviation, if any, gets the same treatment as Matrix Profile.\n\nGo ahead; report STAGE 3/8 DONE with the v0.9.37 commit hash."}
